From: qcom-vp maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] arm: expose the virtual GIC list-register count on TCG max

QHEE writes ICH_LR4_EL2 (S3_4_C12_C12_4) while it programs the virtual GIC for
the guest. Every max TCG core sets gic_num_lrs to four, and the cpu interface
then defines ICH_LR0..LR3 only, so the fifth list register traps as an
unsupported system register and QHEE stops in its unknown-trap handler.

Expose the count as an opt-in property so a profile can state the list-register
capacity it needs. The default keeps the existing value of four.

Source: Arm IHI 0069 (GICv3/v4 architecture), ICH_VTR_EL2.ListRegs.
https://developer.arm.com/documentation/ihi0069/

--- a/target/arm/tcg/cpu64.c
+++ b/target/arm/tcg/cpu64.c
@@ -1172,6 +1172,8 @@
         DEFINE_PROP_BOOL("x-qcom-mpam", ARMCPU, qcom_mpam, false);
     static const Property qcom_ids_property =
         DEFINE_PROP_BOOL("x-qcom-ids", ARMCPU, qcom_ids, false);
+    static const Property qcom_gic_lr_property =
+        DEFINE_PROP_INT32("x-qcom-gic-num-lrs", ARMCPU, gic_num_lrs, 4);
 #endif
     uint64_t t;
     uint32_t u;
@@ -1455,6 +1457,7 @@
 #ifndef CONFIG_USER_ONLY
     qdev_property_add_static(DEVICE(obj), &qcom_mpam_property);
     qdev_property_add_static(DEVICE(obj), &qcom_ids_property);
+    qdev_property_add_static(DEVICE(obj), &qcom_gic_lr_property);
 #endif
 }
 
